      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext"
        },
        "content": "<div style=\"font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;color:#c7d0d9;background:#181b1f;border:1px solid #2c3235;border-left:3px solid #37872D;border-radius:3px;padding:12px 16px;\"><b style=\"color:#e8eaed\">ClusterMinder / CVT &mdash; open worklists.</b><br>The four counters below are the only open fault classes ClusterMinder tracks. Each one is paired with a table built from the <i>identical</i> query, so the number on the tile and the row count in the table beneath it are always the same (the table footer prints its own row count). Tray rows come from the on-tray <code>node-exporter</code> and NVLink collector; switch rows from the <code>switch-fw</code> exporter, which probes every NVLink / InfiniBand / Ethernet switch hourly and is not filtered by the tray pickers.<div style=\"font:12px/1.5 -apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e;margin-top:8px\">ClusterMinder&nbsp;/&nbsp;CVT: <a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/nvis-l2-cvt-clusterminder/x\">Open worklists</a>&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;<a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/cvt-clusterminder-inventory/x\">Inventory &amp; coverage</a>&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;<a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/cvt-clusterminder-config/x\">Firmware &amp; config alignment</a>&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;<a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/cvt-cable-validation/x\">Cable &amp; Layer-1 vs golden</a></div></div>",
